  "schema:description": "The ninth in a series of comprehensive bottom trawl surveys of groundfish resources in the Gulf of Alaska (GOA) region was conducted from May 18 through August 6, 2005, by the Resource Assessment and Conservation Engineering (RACE) Division of the Alaska Fisheries Science Center (AFSC), Seattle, Washington. Since 1999 this survey has been conducted biennially; earlier surveys were conducted triennially between 1984 and 1999.\n\nPurpose: The major survey objective is to continue the time series begun in 1984 to monitor trends in distribution, abundance, and population biology of important groundfish species and to describe and measure various biological and environmental parameters.",
  "schema:creativeWorkStatus": "completed",
